       "position": "relative",
       "children": [
        {
         "id": "a0c8f21",
         "type": "text-editor",
         "cls": "",
         "box": [
          153,
          527,
          540,
          552
         ],
         "gap": "20px",
         "width": "540px",
         "maxWidth": "100%",
         "position": "relative",
         "parts": [
          {
           "tag": "p",
           "box": [
            153,
            527,
            540,
            96
           ],
           "fontFamily": "Poppins",
           "fontSize": "16px",
           "fontWeight": "400",
           "lineHeight": "24px",
           "color": "rgb(46, 46, 46)",
           "width": "540px",
           "marginBottom": "14.4px",
           "text": "A s a teenager, I have always been interested and curious about marriages. I was the child who would sit and watch a marriage teaching on the TV, read a relationship magazine and any article on marriage."
          },
          {
           "tag": "p",
           "box": [
            153,
            637,
            540,
            192
           ],
           "fontFamily": "Poppins",
           "fontSize": "16px",
           "fontWeight": "400",
           "lineHeight": "24px",
           "color": "rgb(46, 46, 46)",
           "width": "540px",
           "marginBottom": "14.4px",
           "text": "I loved seeing happy couples and I felt passionate about relationships. As I became a young adult, I noticed I would get inspiration on building healthy relationships and give advice to friends and strangers, even though I wasn’t married at that time. I knew this was a natural passion God has given "
          },
          {
           "tag": "p",
           "box": [
            153,
            844,
            540,
            72
           ],
           "fontFamily": "Poppins",
           "fontSize": "16px",
           "fontWeight": "400",
           "lineHeight": "24px",
           "color": "rgb(46, 46, 46)",
           "width": "540px",
           "marginBottom": "14.4px",
           "text": "The birth of Ruth’s Marriage officially started on social media a few years ago after I had worked in corporate employment for over 10 years."
          },
          {
           "tag": "p",
           "box": [
            153,
            930,
            540,
            72
           ],
           "fontFamily": "Poppins",
           "fontSize": "16px",
           "fontWeight": "400",
           "lineHeight": "24px",
           "color": "rgb(46, 46, 46)",
           "width": "540px",
           "marginBottom": "14.4px",
           "text": "Our mission at Ruth’s Marriage is to help couples enjoy their marriage by providing them with the right professional and godly counsel and simple actionable tools that yield positive results."
          },
          {
           "tag": "p",
           "box": [
            153,
            1016,
            540,
            48
           ],
           "fontFamily": "Poppins",
           "fontSize": "16px",
           "fontWeight": "400",
           "lineHeight": "24px",
           "color": "rgb(46, 46, 46)",
           "width": "540px",
           "marginBottom": "14.4px",
           "text": "We believe that you can enjoy your marriage and that is why we are here to support you!"
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
